## Converting a PDF source to Markdown
#schema
When a new `.pdf` file appears in `PDFs/`, automatically convert the PDF into a clean Markdown and add it to `sources/` as a `.md` file via the following procedure:

1. Read the PDF.  
2. Convert the full paper into Markdown.  
3. Preserve the paper's structure:  
   - Title  
   - Authors  
   - Abstract  
   - Section headings  
   - Subsections  
   - Paragraphs  
   - Equations  
   - Tables  
   - Footnotes  
   - References  
4. Preserve figure captions in their original location but do not include any text from the figure itself. 
5. Do not summarize or paraphrase any part of the paper. 
6. Do not edit the content of the text even if you believe it to be false.  
7. Do not add commentary.  
8. Do not invent missing content.  
9. Fix obvious PDF line-break and spacing issues so its clear to read.  
10. Remove page headers, footers, and page numbers.  
11. Convert tables to Markdown tables when possible.
12. Keep citations, equations, symbols, and technical terms as accurate as possible.  
13. for any mathmathical equations insert them as images. 
14. If text is unreadable, write `[unreadable]`.
15. Add properties using the format below, if any of the information is unavailable leave it blank.
        `---
        Title: ""
        Author: ""
        Published: YYYY-MM-DD
        Created: YYYY-MM-DD
        Processed: false
        tags:
        - "sources"
        ---`
16. When complete, use [[Extract Figure]] to extract any figures within the PDFs, and then use [[Organize Repo]] to finish the task.